    {
      "id": "i1",
      "content": "To begin the process, the inventory needs to be checked."
    },
    {
      "id": "i2",
      "content": "After that, Mac compares the inventory levels in the spreadsheet with the sales."
    },
    {
      "id": "i3",
      "content": "If the inventory level is high"
    },
    {
      "id": "i4",
      "content": "Mac doesn't need to manually count the inventory."
    },
    {
      "id": "i5",
      "content": "However, if the inventory level is low, Mac needs to manually count the inventory of items."
    },
    {
      "id": "i6",
      "content": "Once Mac counts each item individually"
    },
    {
      "id": "i7",
      "content": "they make a list of items that have a low stock count."
    },
    {
      "id": "i8",
      "content": "Using this list, Mac selects suppliers for the needed products and places the order(s)."
    },
    {
      "id": "i9",
      "content": "After receiving the order, the process comes to an end."
